WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
two matching charges, one purchase.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.680
Before a refund, someone needs to check the evidence.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.880
Resolve helps investigate fictional payment disputes while keeping

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.740
the final refund decision human.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.340
Start with the dashboard.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.980
Choose a customer, inspect the payment history and

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.140
compare the two matching Northstar charges.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.220
Matching records are a signal, not proof.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.840
Attach a payment to an investigation, then review

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.620
your question before sending it.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.840
The Gemini agent searches transactions, explains recorded decline

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.160
codes, and proposes eligible refunds.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.120
It cannot approve them.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.400
Next.js serves the interface and server.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.000
A private PostgREST adapter connects to Neon Postgres.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.180
Integer cents, database locks, and Unique Execution Keys

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.720
protect the mock refund ledger.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.140
Explore the live demo.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.800
Investigate the charge.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.720
Keep the decision human.
